       "code": "def f1(p, g):\n    p, g = normalise(p).split(), normalise(g).split()\n    common = sum(min(p.count(w), g.count(w)) for w in set(p))\n    if common == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    precision, recall = common / len(p), common / len(g)\n    return 2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall)\n\nscores = [f1(p, g) for p, g in zip(pred, gold)]\nprint([round(s, 2) for s in scores])\nprint(round(float(np.mean(scores)), 3))",
       "say": "**Token F1** gives partial credit for overlapping words. Precision: what share of the system's words are in the gold answer; recall: what share of the gold answer's words the system produced; F1 combines them. \"In 1969.\" has one right word of two: 0.67; \"Mt. Everest\" shares \"everest\": 0.5; \"the Pacific\" against \"Pacific Ocean\": precision 1, recall 0.5, so 0.67; \"Marie Curie was the physicist\": 0.67 (the extra words cost precision). The mean is **0.56**, more than twice the EM of 0.25. F1 rewards the overlap but also rewards padding with the right words a little and still scores a synonym (\"water\" for H2O) at **0**: it counts words, not meaning.",
