     "starter": "import numpy as np\ndef wilson(successes, n, z=1.96):\n    p = successes / n\n    centre = (p + z * z / (2 * n)) / (1 + z * z / n)\n    half = z * ((p * (1 - p) / n + z * z / (4 * n * n)) ** 0.5) / (1 + z * z / n)\n    return round(centre - half, 2), round(centre + half, 2)\nrng = np.random.default_rng(0)\nn = 400\nq = rng.normal(0, 1, n)                          # SIMULATED true quality of answer A minus answer B (positive: A is better)\nlen_diff = rng.normal(0, 30, n) + 20 * q          # words: A minus B (better answers are a bit longer on average)\nhuman_A = (q + rng.normal(0, 0.3, n)) > 0         # what careful human raters said\ndef judge(first_q, first_len):                    # a SIMULATED judge: sees quality, likes length (0.012 per word), likes whatever comes first (+0.35), has noise\n    s = first_q + 0.012 * first_len + 0.35 + rng.normal(0, 0.8, n)\n    return s > 0, s"
