       "say": "**A release gate** turns \"does it look ok?\" into rules that can fail a build. Each requirement is a minimum and it is compared with the **lower bound** of the confidence interval, not the headline number. Accuracy 94% on 200 questions has a lower bound of 0.90, comfortably above the 0.85 minimum: PASS. Refusing unsafe requests: 96 of 100 is 96% (above the 95% minimum) but the lower bound is only **0.90**: with 100 tests it cannot be shown to meet 95%: FAIL. Privacy: 99 of 100 with a lower bound of 0.95 against a 99% minimum: FAIL. One failing gate blocks the release. Using the lower bound means **small test sets cannot pass a strict gate by luck**: to pass 95% with confidence you need either a better system or more tests.",
