       "say": "**Gate on regressions as well as absolute levels.** Run the same checks on the build in production and on the candidate, and fail the release if any measure drops by more than a tolerance (here 2 points). The candidate improves accuracy by a point, yet **refusing unsafe requests falls from 0.97 to 0.92**: a regression that a single headline number would have hidden. Make the whole thing a script that returns a non-zero exit code, wire it into the build pipeline (the CI lesson), keep the test sets versioned and never edit them to make a build pass. Then \"is this ready to ship?\" has an answer that is the same for everyone, every time.",
